From acedaec60d430ba73fbd15657b293f25d1eae805 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 10:49:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] Support dragging files and text into client windows

Implement the compositor-to-client half of wl_data_device
drag-and-drop, so that e.g. a file dragged from the Finder onto a
foot window pastes its path.

OwlSurface registers as a Cocoa dragging destination and forwards
the session to the client's wl_data_device following the same
enter/motion/leave/drop shape. The content is wrapped in a new
OwlDragDataSource: filenames become text/uri-list (CRLF-separated
file:// URIs per RFC 2483) with a bare-paths text/plain fallback,
and dragged text is offered as plain text. Unlike the pasteboard
data source, the content is snapshotted up front: clients read the
data asynchronously after the drop, when the drag pasteboard may
already be gone.

The offer rides the existing OwlWlDataOffer machinery, marked as a
drag-and-drop offer: version 3+ clients get source_actions(copy)
and an action(copy) answer to their set_actions, which is all the
negotiation a copy-only source needs. Client-initiated drags
(start_drag) remain unsupported.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G6m1eevhAns3j85HMZYKna
